From 1d2fb9547172eefd8a2b9da311f02ee656b22e97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 02:22:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [EME] Keep the encrypted media API on YouTube with the
 external CDM

https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328385

Reviewed by NOBODY (OOPS!).

YouTube serves some videos to its TV client as Widevine-protected
streams only. The youtube.com quirk for bug 195598 removes
navigator.requestMediaKeySystemAccess() wherever WebKit is built
without Thunder, so YouTube finds no key system and reports that the
video format is not supported. Like Thunder, the external CDM backend
plays Widevine content, so builds with it keep the API on youtube.com.

* Source/WebCore/page/Quirks.cpp:
(WebCore::Quirks::hasBrokenEncryptedMediaAPISupportQuirk const):

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 Source/WebCore/page/Quirks.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/Source/WebCore/page/Quirks.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/page/Quirks.cpp
@@ -327,7 +327,7 @@ bool Quirks::shouldAutoplayWebAudioForAr
 // youtube.com https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=195598
 bool Quirks::hasBrokenEncryptedMediaAPISupportQuirk() const
 {
-#if ENABLE(THUNDER)
+#if ENABLE(THUNDER) || ENABLE(EXTERNAL_CDM)
     return false;
 #else
     QUIRKS_EARLY_RETURN_IF_DISABLED_WITH_VALUE(false);
